      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The craft of the power grid has been severely tested. The system's guardians are contending with a cascade of technical failures, where eleven generators have broken down since May. A major protective disconnection at the Kepco SPC Power plant resulted in a massive 950 MW capacity loss. Simultaneously, extreme summer heat has pushed demand to a precarious operational limit, forcing decision-makers to implement an emergency demand response to prevent the backbone network from overloading. This series of events has cast a long shadow of potential rolling blackouts over the Visayas.",
