    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "In the Visayas archipelago, a critical node in the power network is now under a high-alert status. The cause was a confluence of planned and unplanned shutdowns at aging facilities, which, combined with a heatwave pushing the system into a fragile edge, led to a critical equipment failure at a key generating asset. The resulting energy shortfall triggered an emergency load-shedding protocol. The entire region's grid now faces an elevated risk of systematic power rationing to avert a wider collapse.",
